<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George Washington Goethals</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1858">1858</a>–<a href="/years/1928">1928</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-washington">George Washington</a> Goethals was a US Army engineer who directed the construction of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panama-canal">Panama Canal</a> from 1907 until its opening in August 1914. He reorganised the work, settled on a lock canal and built the Gatun Dam. He then served as the first governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panama-canal-zone">Panama Canal Zone</a> until 1916.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-washington-goethals.jpg" alt="George Washington Goethals" width="320" height="456" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Miscellaneous Items in High Demand, PPOC, Library of Congress · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:George_Washington_Goethals,_in_uniform,_three-quarter_length_portrait,_seated,_facing_right_LCCN92519771_Trim.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
